<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated: 5 November 2026</p>

<p>Your privacy matters to us. This policy explains what personal information Black Rabbit collects through this website and when you contact us, how we use it, and what rights you have. We handle personal data in line with Kenya's Data Protection Act, 2019.</p>

<h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
<p>Black Rabbit, Basic Mall Statehouse, Nakuru, Kenya, is the data controller. Contact us at <a href="mailto:navajkerrie@gmail.com">navajkerrie@gmail.com</a> or +254 712 364 610.</p>

<h2>2. What we collect</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Reservation form:</strong> your name, email address, preferred date and time, number of guests, seating preference, any special occasion, and anything you write in the notes. Please only share what you are comfortable with. If you tell us about access or other personal needs, we use that only to look after you.</li>
<li><strong>Marketing choice:</strong> whether you ticked the optional box to hear from us about events and offers.</li>
<li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> if you message us, we receive your phone number, name and the content of your messages. When you tap the WhatsApp button on this site, we also record that a click happened, along with the page address and the time, so we can see which parts of the site bring enquiries. This record does not include your phone number.</li>
<li><strong>Technical data:</strong> like most websites, the servers that deliver this site and its fonts may receive your IP address, browser type and device details. See our <a href="cookies.html">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How and why we use it</h2>
<ul>
<li>To respond to your table request, confirm or change your booking, and prepare for your visit. This is done at your request, and you give us your consent when you submit the form.</li>
<li>To reply to your messages and questions.</li>
<li>To send you news, events and offers, only if you opted in. You can opt out at any time.</li>
<li>To run, secure and improve the website and the bar, which is in our legitimate interest, and to meet any legal obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>We don't sell your personal data, and we don't use it for automated decisions that significantly affect you.</p>

<h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
<p>We share data only with providers who help us run the business, and only what they need:</p>
<ul>
<li>Website hosting and form or automation tools used to receive and route reservation requests and enquiries.</li>
<li>Email and messaging services, including WhatsApp (Meta), used to confirm bookings and talk to you.</li>
<li>Google Fonts, which delivers the typefaces used on the site.</li>
<li>Authorities or advisers, where the law requires it or to protect our rights.</li>
</ul>
<p>Some of these providers store data on servers outside Kenya. Where that happens, we take steps to make sure your data is protected as the Data Protection Act requires.</p>

<h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
<p>We keep reservation details for as long as needed to manage your booking, and for up to 12 months afterwards in case of questions or disputes, unless the law requires us to keep records longer. Marketing contacts are kept until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them. WhatsApp conversations are kept for as long as they are useful for the enquiry.</p>

<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
<p>Under the Data Protection Act, 2019, you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
<li>be told how your data is used, and ask for a copy of it;</li>
<li>ask us to correct data that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
<li>ask us to delete your data;</li>
<li>object to certain uses of your data, including marketing;</li>
<li>withdraw your consent at any time. This won't affect anything we did before you withdrew it.</li>
</ul>
<p>To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:navajkerrie@gmail.com">navajkerrie@gmail.com</a>. We will reply as soon as we reasonably can. If you are not happy with how we handle your data, you can also complain to the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner of Kenya (<a href="https://www.odpc.go.ke" rel="noopener" target="_blank">odpc.go.ke</a>).</p>

<h2>7. Keeping your data safe</h2>
<p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information, such as limiting who can see it and using trusted providers. No online system is perfectly secure, so we can't guarantee absolute security, but we take it seriously and will act promptly if something goes wrong.</p>

<h2>8. Children</h2>
<p>Black Rabbit is a bar and our website is meant for adults. We don't knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 18. If you think a child has sent us their details, please contact us and we will delete them.</p>

<h2>9. Links to other sites</h2>
<p>This site may link to other services, such as WhatsApp. They have their own privacy policies, and we are not responsible for how they handle your data.</p>

<h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it last changed. If we make a significant change, we will make that clear on the site.</p>

